
{"id":"e6208ed4-c6fa-4162-9f51-d0422fea060f","object":"chat.completion","created":1784837688,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    payload = case['payload']\\n    nodes = payload['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(payload['required_symbols'])\\n    parent_children = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        p = n['parent']\\n        if p is not None:\\n            parent_children.setdefault(p, []).append(n['id'])\\n    retained = set(n['id'] for n in nodes)\\n    symbol_count = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        symbol_count[n['symbol']] = symbol_count.get(n['symbol'], 0) + 1\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    removal_order = []\\n    for n in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = n['id']\\n        if nid not in retained:\\n            continue\\n        if not n['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        if nid == 'root':\\n            continue\\n        children = parent_children.get(nid, [])\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children):\\n            continue\\n        sym = n['symbol']\\n        if sym in required_symbols and symbol_count[sym] == 1:\\n            continue\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        symbol_count[sym] -= 1\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n    return {\\n        'retained_ids': sorted(retained),\\n        'removal_order': removal_order\\n    }\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a Python implementation for `solve(case)` that performs tree reduction based on the given constraints. The problem: given a tree of nodes with parent references, symbols, and utilities, and a list of required symbols, we need to reduce the tree by removing nodes that are removable and not required, while ensuring after removal the tree remains \"grammar valid\" (presumably meaning that all required symbols are still present, and maybe that the tree structure is valid? Actually, the description mentions \"Perse